data/memory.json
# The database plus the -wal/-shm sidecars WAL mode creates alongside it.
data/agentic.db*
# A relative `database_file` resolves against the working directory, so a
# script run from the repository root leaves one here. Runtime data, not
# source, wherever it lands.
/agentic.db*
/sbom.json
vault/
# Backups contain every row of the database, including user data.
backups/
# Course files and anything with personal data (names, student numbers).
# This repository is public: keep them here, where Git never sees them.
# This also covers brain/private/, for second-brain notes that stay local.
private/
# The capstone course package and the team workspace. Both hold course
# files, five members' names and their registration numbers, so neither
# may ever reach this public repository. The team workspace is a separate
# private repository with its own CLAUDE.md, Memory.md and session logs.
inputs/

# Course material and the private review, by name. On 18 October four pull
# requests on this repository's `main` copied all of this out of `private/`
# into the repository root and published it: the 5,000-row course dataset,
# a file holding five registration numbers, teammates' names, and the
# private assessment and its probe output. Ignoring the paths is not what
# fixes that -- only the owner can contain what is already in a public
# history -- but it stops the same upload happening twice. See ADR 0047.
Group_9226_*
Team3_*
/roles/
/PROJECT_ASSESSMENT.md
/REQUIREMENT_EVIDENCE_MATRIX.md
/UI_AGENT_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN_*.md
/ANTHROPIC_AGENTIC_OS_RESEARCH_*.md
/CLAUDE_CODE_UI_AGENTS_HARNESS_PROMPT.md
/AI_Driven_Predictive_Maintenance_SaaS_Playbook.md
/workbook-review.xlsx
